The '''Phase-III Dark Trooper''', also known as the '''third-generation design Dark Trooper''', was a type of elite, experimental [[third-generation battle droid]] manufactured by the [[Imperial Department of Military Research]] and used by the [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|Imperial remnant]] of [[Moff]] [[Gideon]]. The [[Color|black]] and silver-plated [[droid]]s were [[humanoid]] in shape and featured a pair of red [[photoreceptor]]s. 

The droids were heat resistant, blaster resistant, and utilised extreme strength, being able to heavily damage Imperial blast doors- but were very slow in general speed. According to Dr. Penn Pershing, they took up too much energy to be ready at all times, so they were kept in cold storage and took a few minutes to deploy.

==Description==
{{Quote|These are third-generation design. They are no longer suits. The human inside was the final weakness to be solved. They're droids.|[[Penn Pershing]], on the dark troopers|<ref name="Chapter 16" />}}
[[File:The-Mandalorian-dark-troopers.png|thumb|left|275px|Four dark troopers in flight over Tython.]]
Dark trooper armor was originally designed to be worn by human soldiers as a battle suit, but this ended up being a weakness. As such, the third-generation was created as a droid to overcome this weakness.<ref name="SWCEUAE" /> Succeeding the [[Phase II Dark Trooper]]<ref name="PhasesNote">{{SWU|set=Shadows of the Galaxy|cardname=Phase-III Dark Trooper|link=4843225228|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20241227044612/https://www.swudb.com/card/SHD/084/phase-iii-dark-trooper}} establishes that the Phase-III Dark Trooper is the third phase of the [[Dark Trooper project]]. ''[[Star Wars: Commander]]'' features a [[Dark Trooper]] unit known as the [[Phase II Dark Trooper]]. Logically, the Phase-III unit must be the successor to the Phase II unit.</ref> used by the [[Galactic Empire]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]] against the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]],<ref name="Commander">''[[Star Wars: Commander]]''</ref> dark troopers were an elite<ref name="Legion Expansion">{{Legion|set=Dark Troopers Unit Expansion}}</ref> and experimental model of the [[third-generation battle droid]] developed by the [[Imperial Department of Military Research]].<ref name="SWCEUAE" /> Dark troopers were equipped with two [[rocket booster]]s, one in each foot.<ref name="Chapter 14" /> Dark trooper armor was capable of withstanding blaster fire, exposure to a [[flamethrower]], and several strikes from [[whistling bird]]s, but were still vulnerable to [[lightsaber]] strikes, allowing the [[Jedi]] Luke Skywalker to destroy an entire [[platoon]] with [[Luke Skywalker's green lightsaber|his lightsaber]] with relative ease. Their unarmored neck also was a weak point, which Din Djarin exploited after staggering the dark trooper with whistling birds. Dark troopers also possessed extreme strength.<ref name="Chapter 16" />

A single dark trooper was able to pry open the doors to its containment area and could easily pick up Djarin and toss him about. Two dark troopers were able to work together to severely damage a set of [[blast door]]s through repeated strikes, and a single dark trooper was capable of severely damaging a wall of [[Gideon's light cruiser]] by repeatedly striking Djarin's [[beskar]] [[helmet]] and literally embedding him in the wall, but was unable to cave-in the helmet itself. Aside from armor and brute strength, dark troopers also wielded large [[blaster rifle]]s, known as [[E-450 "Arc Hammer" heavy blaster rifle]]s<ref name="MandoVG" /> which they could aim with precision accuracy, as seen when a dark trooper fired several shots at Djarin all of which hit him, but glanced off his beskar armor.<ref name="Chapter 16" /> For even greater efficiency, a force of Dark Troopers could be deployed alongside a [[death trooper]] escort, who would hold command over the battle droids.<ref name="Databank Download">{{AtomicMassGames|url=transmission/databank-download-death-trooper-escort-dark-troopers|text=Databank Download: Death Trooper Escort & Dark Troopers}}</ref>

==History==
In [[9 ABY]], a [[Gideon's Dark Trooper platoon|platoon]] of third-generation [[Dark Trooper|dark troopers]] were held in a cargo bay of [[Gideon's light cruiser]] in cold storage.<ref name="Chapter 16" /> After a [[Second skirmish on Nevarro|skirmish on Nevarro]] caused the destruction of an [[Nevarro Imperial base|Imperial base]], [[Elia Kane]] reported to Moff Gideon, who was overseeing rows of deactivated dark troopers with a group of [[scientist]]s, that a [[homing beacon]] was installed on the ''[[Razor Crest]].''<ref name="Chapter 12">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 12: The Siege}}</ref> After tracking the ''Razor Crest'' to [[Tython]], Gideon had four deployed to the planet's surface to kidnap a [[Force-sensitive]] [[alien]] [[Youngling|child]] known as [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] from his guardian, the [[Mandalorian]] [[Din Djarin]]. The droids succeeded and returned to Gideon's [[light cruiser]] with the youngling.<ref name="Chapter 14" />

[[File:Acme-TheRescue.png|thumb|right|300px|Luke Skywalker enters the hallway leading to the bridge to cut through the Dark Trooper platoon.]]
While [[Second rescue of Grogu|rescuing]] his [[foundling]], Djarin destroyed one of the droids by piercing the droid's unarmored neck with a [[beskar spear]]. Djarin subsequently released the remainder out of the [[airlock]] and into [[Realspace|space]], but returned to the [[cruiser]] via their rocket boosters. They then almost managed to retake the cruiser single-handedly. Mere seconds before they were able to breach the [[Bridge (starship)|bridge]] [[blast door]]s, [[Jedi Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]] arrived. He sliced through them with his lightsaber.<ref name="Chapter 16" /> Following his [[Extraction of Moff Gideon|extraction]] from [[New Republic]] custody,<ref name="Chapter 21">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 21: The Pirate}}</ref> Gideon hid in a [[Mandalore Imperial base|Imperial base]] on the planet [[Mandalore]], where his remnant used Mandalorian resources to create the [[Dark Trooper phase 4|fourth-generation]] of Dark Trooper design: the design returned the Dark Trooper to a suit, which was created from [[beskar]] alloy and worn by Gideon and his clone army.<ref name="Chapter 23">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 23: The Spies}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
===Development===
[[File:DarkTrooper-TMCh16.png|thumb|left|270px|A third-generation Dark Trooper in "Chapter 16: The Rescue"]]
The Phase-III Dark Trooper first appeared in "[[Chapter 12: The Siege]]," the fourth episode of the [[The Mandalorian Season Two|second season]] of the [[Disney+]] live-action series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'',<ref name="Chapter 12" /> which originally aired on [[November 20]], [[2020]].<ref name="D23November">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-november-2020|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in November 2020}}</ref> It was first identified as a "dark trooper" in the audio description available for the episode on Disney+.<ref name="audio description">Per the audio description for "[[Chapter 12: The Siege]]," available on [[Disney+]].</ref> Its full name of "Phase-III Dark Trooper" was first given through the unit's card in the ''[[Shadows of the Galaxy]]'' expansion of ''[[Star Wars: Unlimited]]'', with the card being teased&mdash;and the Phase-III name first given&ndash;through the article "Shadows of the Galaxy" on [[April 3]], [[2024]]. The proper capitalization of "Phase-III Dark Trooper," however, remains speculation.<ref name="SotG">{{UnlimitedWeb|url=articles/shadows-of-the-galaxy|text=Shadows of the Galaxy}}</ref> The alternative names of "third-generation design Dark Trooper"<ref name="Sideshow">{{HotToysCite|set=Television Masterpiece Series|packtype=Sixth Scale Figure|pack=#032: Dark Trooper|link=collectibles/star-wars-dark-trooper-hot-toys-907625}}</ref> and "phase 3 darktrooper"<ref name="DroidsWar">{{EncyclopediaCite|Battle Droids and Other Droids of War}}</ref> were revealed its [[Sideshow Collectibles]] figure<ref name="Sideshow" /> and the reference booklet "[[Battle Droids and Other Droids of War]]," respectively.<ref name="DroidsWar" />

In "[[Chapter 16: The Rescue]],"<ref name="Gallery">{{DisneyGallery|Disney Gallery: The Mandalorian: Making of Season Two|Making of Season Two}}</ref> the ''Mandalorian'' Season Two finale that first debuted on [[December 18]], 2020, on Disney+,<ref name="D23December">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-december-2020|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in December 2020}}</ref> Dark Troopers were realized with stunt actors in a full-body suit and then augmented with CGI. According to the production team, it was the better option for bringing the scene to life and to fit with the style of [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars:'' Episode IV ''A New Hope'']],<ref name="Gallery" /> the first ever ''[[Star Wars]]'' film from [[1977]] that kicked off the ''Star Wars'' franchise.<ref name="YearByYear">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, New Edition]]''</ref>

===Contradictions===
The [[2024]] reference book ''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]'' misidentifies the Phase-III Dark Trooper as the Phase-II,<ref name="CompEncyc">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> a separate model of Dark Trooper first seen in the video game ''[[Star Wars: Commander]]''.<ref name="Commander" />

